implementationPlan.description:
MOVE A, PART 1 — REMOVE THE TWO RESIDUE TEST BLOCKS AND THE 11 RESIDUE TABLE ROWS. Edit surgically. Never `git checkout`/`reset`/`stash` this file: it is clean vs HEAD, so a checkout is a silent no-op that leaves you believing you removed something, and the whole point is a real deletion. Delete exactly three regions, identified BY NAME rather than by line number since earlier deletions shift the rest:
(a) the whole `it("pages only exact event-type matches across an interleaved ledger", ...)` block (currently ~265-273);
(b) the whole `it("returns an honest empty page for an unknown type and refuses an oversized match", ...)` block (currently ~309-323);
(c) inside the `INVALID_READS` table, the ELEVEN rows whose read closure calls `readEventsByTypeAfter` — `empty event type`, `NUL event type`, `oversized event type`, `ill-formed event type`, `non-string event type`, `negative type cursor`, `non-bigint type cursor`, `zero type limit`, `1001 type limit`, `zero type bytes`, `oversized type bytes` — plus the comment line that belongs to them, `// eventType is validated first, so a valid type proves the cursor layer refused.`
DO NOT TOUCH, and verify each survives byte-exact afterwards:
- `it("reports the exact event horizon and observes a later append", ...)` (~145-175) — this is task-d92's work, the reason this file must be edited rather than reverted;
- `it("serves both event-type page phases from the composite index", ...)` (~325-349) — MEASURED CLEAN. It contains ZERO `readEventsByTypeAfter` references and produces ZERO baseline typecheck errors; it exercises `EVENT_TYPE_PAGE_CANDIDATE_QUERY` / `EVENT_TYPE_PAGE_MATERIALIZE_QUERY` against the real `domain_events_event_type_position` index landed by task-d20ffd07 (commit 77e037c). It is landed foreign work, NOT residue. Deleting it would destroy another task's deliverable — the exact failure the task rail warns about;
- the 19 surviving `INVALID_READS` rows and the `for (const [name, run, code, detail] of INVALID_READS)` generator;
- `packages/store/src/event-read-query.ts` — do not open it to edit; it must stay byte-identical.

MOVE A, PART 2 — SWEEP THE CONSTANTS THE DELETION JUST ORPHANED. This step is NOT optional cleanup: `tsconfig.base.json:17-18` sets `noUnusedLocals: true` and `noUnusedParameters: true`, so a residue removal that stops at step 2 leaves `pnpm --filter @moe/store typecheck` STILL red — 22 TS2551/TS7006 errors simply become a fresh crop of TS6133 errors and DoD 1 fails. Remove these seven, whose ONLY remaining consumers were the regions deleted in step 2 (each verified by grep before this plan was written):
- `seedMixed` (function, ~70) — called only at the two deleted `it` blocks;
- `typeTally` (function, ~85) — called only inside deleted block (a);
- `MIXED_TYPES` (~37) — read only by `ALPHA` and inside `seedMixed`;
- `ALPHA` (~38) — read only by deleted blocks and deleted table rows;
- `MIXED_COUNT` (~39) — read only inside `seedMixed`;
- `BAD_TYPE` (~40) — read only by five deleted table rows;
- `TINY_BYTES` (~41) — read only inside deleted block (b).
MUST SURVIVE, because live consumers remain: `EVENT_TYPE_INDEX` (~42, used by the preserved composite-index test); `OVER_BYTES` (~28, used by three surviving `oversized ... bytes` rows); `BAD_ID` (~33, used by the three surviving id rows and nothing else deleted). Also re-check the import block at the top of the file: remove an import only if it is genuinely unreferenced after the sweep, and leave every import the preserved composite-index test still needs (`DatabaseSync`, `mkdtempSync`, `rmSync`, `join`, `tmpdir`, `EVENT_TYPE_PAGE_CANDIDATE_QUERY`, `EVENT_TYPE_PAGE_MATERIALIZE_QUERY`). Drive this by compiler output, not by eye: iterate `pnpm --filter @moe/store typecheck` until it exits 0, and treat any TS6133 naming a symbol NOT in the seven above as a signal you deleted too much — restore it rather than deleting its consumer.
